gartner-hypecycle-graph: 1
# A hand-authored hype cycle of the technologies around coal, from the Newcomen engine to what
# may follow the phase-out. Dates after 2026 are projections, and dates and influences are
# illustrative, not a claim: see readme.md.
trends:
  - id: newcomen-engine
    name: Newcomen pumping engine
    start: 1712-01
    stop: 1800-01
    row: 0
    phases: 4
    tags: [mining, steam]
    description: Pumped water out of flooded coal mines; the first practical steam engine.
  - id: safety-lamp
    name: Miner's safety lamp
    start: 1815-01
    stop: 1900-01
    row: 2
    phases: 4
    tags: [mining, safety]
    description: Davy's and Stephenson's lamps of 1815, which let miners work among firedamp.
  - id: mechanised-coal-cutting
    name: Mechanised coal cutting
    start: 1880-01
    stop: 1960-01
    row: 0
    phases: 4
    tags: [mining]
  - id: surface-mining
    name: Surface mining
    start: 1920-01
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 2
    phases: 4
    tags: [mining]
    description: Draglines and shovels stripping the ground above shallow seams.
  - id: longwall-mining
    name: Powered longwall mining
    start: 1950-01
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 4
    phases: 4
    tags: [mining]
    description: A shearer runs along the coal face under self-advancing roof supports.
  - id: mountaintop-removal
    name: Mountaintop removal
    start: 1970-01
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 0
    phases: 3
    tags: [mining, environment]
  - id: autonomous-mining
    name: Autonomous mining
    start: 2008-01
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 6
    phases: 2
    tags: [mining, automation]
    description: Driverless haul trucks and remotely run longwalls.
  - id: coke-smelting
    name: Coke iron smelting
    start: 1709-01
    stop: 1800-01
    row: 8
    phases: 4
    tags: [iron]
    description: Abraham Darby smelted iron with coke instead of charcoal at Coalbrookdale in 1709.
  - id: watt-steam-engine
    name: Watt steam engine
    start: 1776-03
    stop: 1850-01
    row: 10
    phases: 4
    tags: [steam]
    description: A separate condenser made the steam engine efficient enough to use anywhere.
  - id: coal-gas-lighting
    name: Coal gas lighting
    start: 1812-04
    stop: 1960-01
    row: 12
    phases: 4
    tags: [gas]
    description: Town gas made by heating coal lit streets and homes for a century and a half.
  - id: steamships
    name: Steamships
    start: 1819-01
    stop: 1950-01
    row: 8
    phases: 4
    tags: [steam, transport]
  - id: steam-locomotive
    name: Steam locomotive
    start: 1825-09
    stop: 1960-01
    row: 14
    phases: 4
    peak-end: 1846-01
    tags: [steam, transport]
    description: From the Stockton and Darlington railway on; railway mania peaked in 1845.
  - id: coal-tar-chemistry
    name: Coal tar chemistry
    start: 1856-03
    stop: 1950-01
    row: 10
    phases: 4
    tags: [chemistry]
    description: Perkin's mauveine turned the gasworks' waste tar into dyes, drugs and explosives.
  - id: coal-power-stations
    name: Coal-fired power stations
    start: 1882-01
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 16
    phases: 4
    tags: [power]
    description: From Holborn Viaduct and Pearl Street in 1882.
  - id: electrostatic-precipitators
    name: Electrostatic precipitators
    start: 1907-01
    stop: 1990-01
    row: 18
    phases: 4
    tags: [environment, power]
    description: Frederick Cottrell's electrified plates pulled fly ash out of the flue gas.
  - id: pulverised-coal-firing
    name: Pulverised coal firing
    start: 1918-01
    stop: 2000-01
    row: 20
    phases: 4
    tags: [power]
  - id: supercritical-boilers
    name: Supercritical boilers
    start: 1957-01
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 22
    phases: 4
    tags: [power]
    description: Steam above its critical point, from Philo 6 in 1957 to ultra-supercritical plants.
  - id: flue-gas-desulfurisation
    name: Flue-gas desulfurisation
    start: 1970-01
    stop: 2026-01
    row: 24
    phases: 4
    tags: [environment, power]
    description: Scrubbers against acid rain, required by clean air laws from 1970 on.
  - id: fluidised-bed-combustion
    name: Fluidised bed combustion
    start: 1975-01
    stop: 2020-01
    row: 26
    phases: 3
    tags: [power]
  - id: igcc
    name: Integrated gasification combined cycle
    start: 1984-01
    stop: 2025-01
    row: 28
    phases: 2
    tags: [power, gasification]
    description: Gasify the coal first, then burn the gas in a turbine; from Cool Water in 1984.
  - id: coal-hydrogenation
    name: Coal hydrogenation
    start: 1913-01
    stop: 1950-01
    row: 30
    phases: 3
    tags: [liquids]
    description: Friedrich Bergius's process for turning coal into oil.
  - id: fischer-tropsch
    name: Fischer-Tropsch coal-to-liquids
    start: 1925-01
    stop: 2020-01
    row: 32
    phases: 4
    tags: [liquids, gasification]
  - id: coal-gasification
    name: Coal gasification
    start: 1931-01
    stop: 2020-01
    row: 34
    phases: 4
    tags: [gasification]
    description: The Lurgi gasifier of 1931 and its successors, making synthesis gas from coal.
  - id: underground-coal-gasification
    name: Underground coal gasification
    start: 1933-01
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 36
    phases: 2
    tags: [gasification]
    description: Gasifying a seam where it lies, tried in the Soviet Union from the 1930s.
  - id: coal-to-chemicals
    name: Coal-to-chemicals
    start: 2004-01
    stop: 2035-01
    row: 30
    phases: 2
    tags: [chemistry, gasification]
    description: China's plants making methanol, olefins and fertiliser from coal.
  - id: smoke-abatement
    name: Smoke abatement
    start: 1853-01
    stop: 1970-01
    row: 38
    phases: 4
    tags: [environment, policy]
    description: From London's Smoke Nuisance Act of 1853 to the Clean Air Act after the Great Smog of 1952.
  - id: carbon-capture-and-storage
    name: Carbon capture and storage
    start: 2005-01
    stop: 2045-01
    row: 38
    phases: 2
    peak-end: 2015-12
    tags: [climate, power]
    description: Capturing a coal plant's carbon dioxide and burying it; most projects stalled after 2015.
  - id: mine-water-heat
    name: Mine water heat
    start: 2008-10
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 40
    phases: 2
    tags: [heat, reuse]
    description: Flooded mines as heat stores, as in Heerlen since 2008.
  - id: coal-phase-out
    name: Coal phase-out
    start: 2017-11
    stop: 2045-01
    row: 42
    phases: 1
    tags: [climate, policy]
    description: Governments committing to close their coal plants, from the Powering Past Coal Alliance on.
  - id: coal-to-hydrogen
    name: Coal to hydrogen with capture
    start: 2021-01
    stop: 2040-01
    row: 44
    phases: 1
    tags: [gasification, climate, upcoming]
    description: Hydrogen gasified from coal, with its carbon dioxide captured.
  - id: coal-plant-repowering
    name: Coal plants repowered
    start: 2021-06
    stop: 2045-01
    row: 46
    phases: 1
    tags: [power, reuse, upcoming]
    description: Old coal sites reused for reactors and batteries, keeping their grid connection.
  - id: critical-minerals-from-coal-ash
    name: Critical minerals from coal ash
    start: 2026-01
    stop: 2042-01
    row: 48
    phases: 1
    tags: [mining, reuse, conceptual]
    description: Rare earths and lithium recovered from a century of ash ponds.
  - id: coal-to-carbon-materials
    name: Coal to carbon materials
    start: 2027-01
    stop: 2045-01
    row: 50
    phases: 1
    tags: [chemistry, conceptual]
    description: Coal as the feedstock for graphite, carbon fibre and graphene instead of fuel.
  - id: direct-carbon-fuel-cells
    name: Direct carbon fuel cells
    start: 2030-01
    stop: 2048-01
    row: 52
    phases: 1
    tags: [power, conceptual]
    description: Turning carbon into electricity electrochemically, without burning it.
triggers:
  - id: rainhill-trials
    name: Rainhill trials
    date: 1829-10
    row: 13
    tags: [steam, transport]
    description: Stephenson's Rocket won the trials for the Liverpool and Manchester Railway, and with them the case for the steam locomotive.
  - id: pearl-street-station
    name: Pearl Street Station opens
    date: 1882-09
    row: 15
    tags: [power]
    description: Edison's first commercial central power station, in Manhattan, burned coal to light the streets around it.
  - id: great-smog
    name: Great Smog of London
    date: 1952-12
    row: 37
    tags: [environment, policy]
    description: Five days of coal smoke trapped under fog in London; thousands died, and the Clean Air Act followed in 1956.
  - id: us-clean-air-act
    name: US Clean Air Act
    date: 1970-12
    row: 23
    tags: [environment, policy]
    description: Federal limits on sulphur dioxide made scrubbers a condition of building a coal plant.
  - id: oil-crisis-1973
    name: 1973 oil crisis
    date: 1973-10
    row: 33
    tags: [policy, liquids]
    description: The oil embargo made fuels and gas made from coal look strategic again.
  - id: paris-agreement
    name: Paris Agreement
    date: 2015-12
    row: 41
    tags: [climate, policy]
    description: The goal of holding warming well below two degrees put a date on unabated coal power.
  - id: felling-disaster
    name: Felling mine disaster
    date: 1812-05
    row: 1
    tags: [mining, safety]
    description: An explosion of firedamp killed 92 at Felling colliery and led to the call for a safe lamp.
  - id: liverpool-manchester-railway
    name: Liverpool and Manchester Railway opens
    date: 1830-09
    row: 15
    tags: [steam, transport]
    description: The first intercity railway worked entirely by steam locomotives.
  - id: mauveine
    name: Perkin makes mauveine
    date: 1856-03
    row: 9
    tags: [chemistry]
    description: A dye made by accident from coal tar, and the start of the synthetic dye industry.
notes:
  - id: note-projections
    text: |-
      Everything drawn after 2026 is a projection, not a record.
      See the readme.
    at: 2042-01
    row: 40
    width: 260
    height: 80
